    "title": "Angrakha Kameez: The Silhouette Everyone's Wearing In 2026",
    "excerpt": "Tracing the royal history and modern resurrection of the wrap-style Angrakha kameez as the ultimate statement festive outfit.",
    "content": "# Angrakha Kameez: The Silhouette Everyone's Wearing In 2026\n\nOriginally worn in royal Mughal courts, the **Angrakha** is instantly recognizable by its diagonal crossover front panel fastened with delicate cords (dori) and handmade fabric tassels (latkans).\n\n## Why the Angrakha Endures\nThe diagonal wrap naturally creates an elongated V-neckline that flatters every frame. Combined with a flared Anarkali-style panel or a tailored straight cut, it brings an unmistakable aura of royalty and regal grace.\n\n## Modern Innovations in 2026\nContemporary Pakistani designers have streamlined the Angrakha for modern wearability:\n- **Lighter Fabrics**: Organza, pure chiffons, and raw silk replace cumbersome velvets for effortless comfort.\n- **Subtle Fastenings**: Hand-braided silk cords with pearl drops instead of heavy metal toggles.\n- **Coordinated Dupattas**: Gossamer net dupattas finished with fine kiran edging.",
